{"command": "cd /etc/nginx/sites-available && cat > workstation-upshalter << 'EOF'
server {
    server_name workstation.upshalter.com;
    access_log /var/log/nginx/workstation-access.log;
    error_log /var/log/nginx/workstation-error.log;

    # Workspace (port 3000)
    location /hermes/workspace/ {
        rewrite ^/hermes/workspace(/.*)$ $1 break;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400;
    }

    # Kanban (port 3001)
    location /hermes/kanban/ {
        rewrite ^/hermes/kanban(/.*)$ $1 break;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3001;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection 'upgrade';
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_cache_bypass $http_upgrade;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400;
    }

    # Orchestrator API (port 8000)
    location /hermes/api/ {
        rewrite ^/hermes/api(/.*)$ $1 break;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header X-API-Key "hma_kUjTtoP_NUBD9EAxlpIjedkc7aNnKYZ1XbgN4_vAjf0";
        proxy_read_timeout 300s;
        proxy_connect_timeout 75s;
    }

    # WebSocket
    location /hermes/ws {
        rewrite ^/hermes/ws(.*)$ /ws$1 break;
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:8000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "Upgrade";
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Real-IP $remote_addr;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_read_timeout 86400;
    }

    # Documentation
    location /hermes/docs/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/docs/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/docs/index.html;
        location ~* \.(js|css|png|jpg|jpeg|gif|ico|svg)$ {
            expires 1y;
            add_header Cache-Control "public, immutable";
        }
    }

    # Dashboard (Workforce Command Center)
    location /hermes/dashboard/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/dashboard/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/dashboard/index.html;
    }

    # Profile page
    location /hermes/profile/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/profile/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/profile/index.html;
    }

    # Skills page
    location /hermes/skill/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/skill/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/skill/index.html;
    }

    # Tools page
    location /hermes/tool/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/tool/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/tool/index.html;
    }

    # Arsify - Shared Knowledge Pool
    location /hermes/arsify/ {
        alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/arsify/;
        try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/arsify/index.html;
    }

    # Redirect /hermes/ to /hermes/docs/
    location = /hermes/ {
        return 301 /hermes/docs/;
    }

    # Health check
    location /health {
        access_log off;
        return 200 "OK\n";
        add_header Content-Type text/plain;
    }

    listen 443 ssl;
    ssl_certificate /etc/letsencrypt/live/workstation.upshalter.com/fullchain.pem;
    ssl_certificate_key /etc/letsencrypt/live/workstation.upshalter.com/privkey.pem;
    include /etc/letsencrypt/options-ssl-nginx.conf;
    ssl_dhparam /etc/letsencrypt/ssl-dhparams.pem;
}

server {
    if ($host = workstation.upshalter.com) {
        return 301 https://$host$request_uri;
    }
    listen 80;
    server_name workstation.upshalter.com;
    return 404;
}
EOF
echo "✅ Config rewritten" && nginx -t 2>&1 | head -10"}

messages.reasoning:
The 404 might be because the alias directive might not be working correctly, or the index.html files are not being served. Let's check if the files exist and check Nginx error log. Also, ensure that the location blocks are correctly defined. The alias directive should point to the directory with trailing slash. We have:

location /hermes/profile/ {
    alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/profile/;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/profile/index.html;
}

But note: when using alias, the location path is replaced by the alias path. For try_files, we need to be careful. Usually, for alias, you might need to use:

try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/profile/index.html;

But the URI after alias is transformed. Actually, the common pattern is:

location /hermes/profile/ {
    alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/profile/;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/profile/index.html;
}

But the try_files might not work as expected because $uri is the original URI. Better to use:

try_files $uri $uri/ =404;

But we want to fallback to index.html for SPA. The typical approach for SPA with alias is:

location /hermes/profile/ {
    alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/profile/;
    index index.html;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/profile/index.html;
}

Actually, the fallback path should be the absolute path or the URI? In the docs location, we used:

location /hermes/docs/ {
    alias /var/www/workstation/hermes/docs/;
    try_files $uri $uri/ /hermes/docs/index.html;
...
}

And that works (HTTP 200). So why profile returns 404? Let's check if the file exists.

Let's examine the file existence and permissions. Also, check Nginx error log.

